		{"id":"a3","type":"text","text":"**Module 01 · Phase 3**\nMutation Self-Validation\nmulti-round self-healing (≤3) · kill δ ≥ 1.0 · C_struct ≥ 1.0\n+ adversarial red-team tier (P3, simulated)","x":-180,"y":-540,"width":340,"height":180},
		{"id":"a4","type":"text","text":"**Module 01 · Phase 4**\nPBCTS — LTLf progression → constructive trace synthesis\nBDA alignment · IDCD convergence gate · SCSL self-correction\n→ Formal Reliability Certificate v2.0 (pure Python, no SPOT)","x":240,"y":-540,"width":360,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b1","type":"text","text":"**Module 02 · Extraction**\nPython AST → **WIR** (Workflow Intermediate Representation)\nJSON CFG — `shared_schemas/wir_schema.json`\n+ **call-order WIR** (D2, `call_order_view.py`): driver-function lifting, sibling calls as task boundaries — the view M03's lifter actually needs","x":-1020,"y":220,"width":360,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b2","type":"text","text":"**V3 · Structural**\nAST / dominator validation\nHARD GATE (abort=True)","x":-580,"y":60,"width":300,"height":120},
		{"id":"b3","type":"text","text":"**V2 · Symbolic**\nZ3 bounded concolic execution\n(≈ no contribution on current corpus)","x":-580,"y":440,"width":300,"height":120},
		{"id":"b5","type":"text","text":"**Confidence Certificate**\nself-mode: combined = 1 − (1−v1)(1−v2)\ndifferential mode: combined = v1\nV3 gates · acceptance ≥ 0.95","x":240,"y":220,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"infra","type":"text","text":"**Infra:** docker-compose — 4 services: `spec-engine`, `extract-engine`, `equiv-engine` (all real FastAPI services), `ui-engine` (only host-exposed port, 8501).\n**CI (PR #80):** per-module test jobs + a real docker-compose startup check.\n**Contract:** WIR schema is the producer/consumer contract between Module 02 and Module 03.","x":700,"y":440,"width":820,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b4","type":"text","text":"**V1 · Dynamic**\nPEP 669 `sys.monitoring` differential tracing\nvs WIR reference interpreter\n(strict / task_only modes)","x":-430,"y":220,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"c3","type":"text","text":"**Module 03 · Phase D — Model Check (canonical: `process_wir_batch`)**\nSynchronous product vs ¬properties → emptiness\n→ **COMPLIANT / VIOLATION / INCONCLUSIVE + readable counterexample**\nAlive-extension LTLf→LTL bridge (`spot::from_ltlf`, De Giacomo–Vardi) + mutual-exclusion edge closure for non-looping automata (PR #70); atom-matching gate → INCONCLUSIVE (PR #67)\nEQI gate: full / conservative / refuse (from M02 confidence)","x":1640,"y":-200,"width":400,"height":340,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d1","type":"text","text":"**Module 04 — Verification Portal**\nStreamlit UI · port 8501 (only exposed service)\ndashboard + one page per engine — all three engines called over HTTP (equiv page fixed via PR #74: `POST /lift`)","x":1640,"y":260,"width":360,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# VibeCheck — Verified Translation Validation\nPost-hoc formal verification: does LLM-generated Python workflow code conform to its originating BPMN 2.0 specification?\n**Snapshot: 2026-07-30, `main-demo` @ `5c65046` — FINAL implementation (end-to-end wired).**","x":-1400,"y":-840,"width":560,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"note-independence","type":"text","text":"**Key design decision — dual-track independence**\nModule 01 never sees the generated code; Module 02 never sees the BPMN diagram. The tracks only meet at Module 03 as independently produced mathematical objects. This avoids circular verification (the spec quietly bending to match the code). Preserved even in the bridge: `property_ingest.py` *ports* Module 01's LTLf normalization rather than importing its source.","x":-680,"y":-840,"width":720,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"e2e","type":"text","text":"**End-to-end demo + eval (PRs #76–78)**\n`demo/e2e_demo.py`: BPMN → M01 → M02 → M03 → verdict + counterexample, on real FLOW-BENCH LLM implementations.\n`demo/eval_e2e/`: mutation-based E2E harness — abstention 0.462, detection 0.357, false-alarm 0.000, cx quality 0.800 (small n, CIs reported).","x":2160,"y":80,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c1","type":"text","text":"**Module 03 · Phase A — Lifter**\ncall-order WIR → Labeled Transition System\nname matching: exact → edit-distance → Sentence-BERT (live in C++ via embedded pybind11)\n(Python ✅ / C++ SPOT ✅)","x":510,"y":-180,"width":380,"height":180},
		{"id":"c2","type":"text","text":"**Module 03 · Phases B–C**\nDivergence-sensitive stuttering bisimulation\n(G–V refinement + spot::scc_info τ-cycle collapse)\n+ isomorphism-based behavioral clustering\n(Python ✅ / C++ ✅ — `process_wir_batch()`)","x":1020,"y":0,"width":380,"height":220},
		{"id":"ingest","type":"text","text":"**Module 03 · Property Ingestion (PR #72)**\n`property_ingest.py` loads `module_03_input.json`\ntier-gates (node()-free P1 only — 17.6% of tier; P0/P2/P3 excluded with reasons) · de-dupes · normalizes LTLf → SPOT infix (\"Option B\": `start(T)`/`done(T)` → one flat **quoted** atom)","x":1190,"y":-550,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"}
